    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">55 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Concurrency</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Asked at Amazon, Walmart, Razorpay</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Thread-Safe Singleton, Double-Checked Locking &amp; Immutability</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">See exactly why double-checked locking without <code>volatile</code> can hand out a half-built object, fix it four ways (volatile, holder, enum, <code>std::call_once</code>), then learn the easier strategy behind all of them: immutable objects, safe publication and copy-on-write snapshots.</p>\n"
